menu "Rive runtime"

    config RIVE_TEXT
        bool "Text (HarfBuzz + SheenBidi)"
        default y
        help
            Builds Rive's text engine with HarfBuzz (shaping) and SheenBidi
            (bidirectional text). Fonts are embedded in the .riv file; glyphs
            are drawn as ordinary paths. Adds roughly 1 MB of code.

    config RIVE_LAYOUT
        bool "Layouts (Yoga)"
        default y
        help
            Builds Rive's layout engine (Yoga flexbox). Without it, layout
            components keep their unlaid-out positions.

    config RIVE_AUDIO
        bool "Audio (miniaudio)"
        default y
        help
            Builds Rive's audio engine (miniaudio: MP3 / WAV / FLAC / Vorbis
            decoding and mixing) so audio events in a .riv play. Built as
            an external engine: no audio device inside miniaudio; the app
            pulls mixed samples (see Rive player > Audio output).

    config RIVE_SCRIPTING
        bool "Scripting (Luau)"
        default y
        help
            Runs the scripts a .riv carries (Rive's Luau scripting): the
            Luau VM, plus libhydrogen to check the editor's signature on
            them. Scripts arrive compiled, so no compiler is built.
            Scripts that decode image bytes, or use the GPU canvas API,
            aren't supported.

    config RIVE_SCRIPTING_REQUIRE_SIGNED
        bool "Only run signed scripts"
        default n
        depends on RIVE_SCRIPTING
        help
            Drops scripts whose signature (added by the Rive editor on
            export) doesn't verify. Off: all scripts run, as in the
            editor.

endmenu
